  "id": "Compound::DB00934 - Gene::1133",
  "verbalization": "Maprotiline, a monoamine oxidase inhibitor, is shown to bind to Chrm4, a receptor involved in the regulation of acetylcholine signaling. This binding leads to Chrm4 participating in various receptor activities, including G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity, neurotransmitter receptor activity, and muscarinic acetylcholine receptor activity. These activities are ultimately linked to Chrm5, suggesting that Maprotiline may influence the function of Chrm5 through its interaction with Chrm4. The evidence indicates a potential mechanism where Maprotiline modulates Chrm4, which in turn affects Chrm5 through a series of receptor-mediated pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Chrm4 as a critical mediator in the relationship between Maprotiline and Chrm5, emphasizing the importance of receptor interactions in drug-target mechanisms.",
